CORE
main.c
--generate-function-body stop --generate-function-body-options assume-false --full-slice
^\[main.assertion.1\] line \d+ before the call: SUCCESS$
^\[main.assertion.2\] line \d+ only reachable with i != 2: SUCCESS$
^VERIFICATION SUCCESSFUL$
^EXIT=0$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
--
The full slicer must keep the call of a function that does not return, here
because its body is ASSUME false: removing the call makes the second assertion
reachable with i == 2.
